  "id": "self-desensitization",
  "term": "self-desensitization",
  "definition": "Self-desensitization is a reduced response to a stimulus after that same stimulus has been applied before. In this source, the tingling caused by an alkylamide became weaker when the applications were separated by about 30 minutes, showing decreased sensitivity to the compound itself over time.",
